ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":112,"prev":114,"next":116,"titles":119,"firmware":32},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":20,"status":21,"firmware":22,"facts":27,"procedures":57,"parameters":69,"related":88,"body":94,"sources":95,"official_url":37,"controls":105},"instrument.track-sends","Track sends to aux out, tape, FX I and FX II (M3 + shift)",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"sends","send levels","fx send","reverb send","delay send","tape send","aux send","aux out","instrument",35,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/track-sends.md",{"modes":17,"screens":18},[13],[19],"M3","Holding `shift` on `M3` turns the encoders into the track's four send levels — to the aux output, to the tape track and to the FX I and FX II send effects.","current",{"min":23,"changed_in":24,"guide_version":25,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[28,34,39,43,47,52],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":32,"confidence":33},"where","Holding `shift` while `M3` is open brings up a white card of four send rows, worked by `E1`…`E4` from the top — aux out (a plug icon), tape (a reel icon), FX I and FX II; a row reads no send at zero.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#23-filter-instrument-m3","1.1.33","verified",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":38},"aux-out","Aux out feeds the external audio track (auxiliary `T5`), whose output leaves through the multi-out jack when that jack is set to audio.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#external-audio","derived",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":42,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":38},"tape","The tape send makes the track's audio available to the tape track (auxiliary `T6`), which replays and mangles it.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#tape",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":32,"confidence":33},"tape-default","In a new project every instrument track's tape send reads 99 (the other sends differ by sound); the tape is the normal path for a track's audio, so 99 there takes nothing away from the mix.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#11-a-new-projects-sounds",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":50,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"fx","FX I and FX II are the two send-effect tracks (auxiliary `T7` and `T8`); what the send does depends on the effect loaded there.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#fx-i-and-fx-ii","official",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":55,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":56},"midi-ccs","Over MIDI, CC36–39 set the four sends in the same order.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#33-instrument-tracks-18-synth-drum-sampler-multisampler-engines","community-verified",[58],{"id":59,"goal":60,"preconditions":61,"steps":64,"result":26,"source":68,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"fx-send","Send part of a track to the FX I effect",[62,63],"instrument mode","the track is selected",[65,66],{"keys":19,"note":26,"set":26},{"keys":67,"note":26,"set":26},"shift + turn E3","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#filter",[70,75,79,83],{"screen":19,"encoder":71,"layer":72,"keys":73,"name":12,"range":26,"default":26,"cc":74,"cc_confidence":56,"note":26,"source":68,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"E1","shift","shift + turn E1",36,{"screen":19,"encoder":76,"layer":72,"keys":77,"name":40,"range":26,"default":26,"cc":78,"cc_confidence":56,"note":26,"source":68,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"E2","shift + turn E2",37,{"screen":19,"encoder":80,"layer":72,"keys":67,"name":81,"range":26,"default":26,"cc":82,"cc_confidence":56,"note":26,"source":68,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"E3","fx i",38,{"screen":19,"encoder":84,"layer":72,"keys":85,"name":86,"range":26,"default":26,"cc":87,"cc_confidence":56,"note":26,"source":68,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":51},"E4","shift + turn E4","fx ii